{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellSlotAlignment","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.operator_ladder_below_pairwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.operator_ladder_below_pairwise","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L315-L320","doc":"And the corpus block-trace operator is flatter still — flatter even than the\npairwise ratio `2`, using the complete-graph ladder `M(3) = 1.78578`,\n`M(4) = 2.11435` of the GAP-10 witness. With `ame_ratio_below_universal` this\norders the three: operator `1.18` < nature `3.42` < universal `5`, so the\nexternal number widens the ladder gap rather than closing it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.ame_ratio_below_universal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.ame_ratio_below_universal","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L307-L313","doc":"The nuclear ladder sits *below* the universal ratio: with the corpus's\nAME-derived `ρ_strong = (1, 3.8128, 13.0316)` one has `M(4) < 5·M(3)`, i.e.\n`B(⁴He)/B(³H) ≈ 3.42` against the zero-range universal `5`. Nuclear binding is\nnot in the universal regime — finite-range effects shift it, exactly as the\nsource states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.two_mu3_add_mu4_neg_of_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.two_mu3_add_mu4_neg_of_flat","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L294-L301","doc":"**A ladder flatter than ratio 2 has a negative three-body moment.** Recorded\nbecause the corpus block-trace operator measures `M(4) < 2·M(3)` under both bond\nconventions, which by `four_sub_two_mul_three` pins `2·μ₃ + μ₄ < 0` — a\ndiagnosis of the operator's ladder, not of nature's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.universal_ratio_not_in_tjon_baseline","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.universal_ratio_not_in_tjon_baseline","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L281-L292","doc":"**The universal ratio is unreachable on the baseline.** A ladder with `μ₄ = 0`,\npositive `μ₂` and positive `M(3)` cannot satisfy `M(4) = 5·M(3)`. Hence the EFT's\n\"no four-body parameter at leading order\" and the simplex's `μ₄ = 0` are\ninequivalent conditions, and a nonzero `μ₄` cannot be read as four-body physics\non the strength of the former. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.tjon_baseline_lt_four_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.tjon_baseline_lt_four_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L273-L279","doc":"**The `μ₄ = 0` baseline is strictly below ratio 4.** For any positive `μ₂`\nthe two-point prediction satisfies `M(4) < 4·M(3)`, whatever `μ₃` is. The bound\ndoes not constrain `μ₃` at all: the gap is exactly `−6·μ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.universal_ratio_forces_mu4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.universal_ratio_forces_mu4","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L258-L265","doc":"**What the simplex basis assigns to a calculation carrying no four-body\ninput.** If a ladder realises the universal four-to-three ratio `M(4) = 5·M(3)`,\nthen its four-body moment is `μ₄ = 9·μ₂ + μ₃` — determined entirely by the\n*lower* moments, with no four-body input anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.four_sub_two_mul_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.four_sub_two_mul_three","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L251-L256","doc":"The gap between `M(4)` and twice `M(3)`. Pure bookkeeping, recorded because\nit is what lets a measured ladder be read back as a sign statement about `μ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.ladder_ratio_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.ladder_ratio_neg","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L193-L197","doc":"The normalised ladder is sign-blind for the same reason, which is why the\nflatness finding survives the convention correction while the sign claims do\nnot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.fracTjon_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.fracTjon_neg","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L177-L191","doc":"**The fractional Tjon deviation is BLIND to a global sign flip.** Negating the\nwhole ladder negates the numerator and the denominator alike, so the score is\nunchanged.\n\nThis is not a curiosity — it is a trap, and it caught this session. The score was\nused to argue that the operator \"matches nature's sign\", and separately that the\nmatch was \"fake because the operator's ladder is globally negative\". **Both\narguments are vacuous**: a quantity invariant under the flip can neither confirm\nnor refute the sign convention. Only the *ladder growth* discriminates, and that\nis likewise sign-blind, which is why it survived when the sign claims did not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.fracTjon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.fracTjon","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L174-L175","doc":"The fractional Tjon deviation of a ladder `(M₂, M₃, M₄)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_target_exceeds_35_percent_of_B4He","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_target_exceeds_35_percent_of_B4He","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L161-L165","doc":"The same target as a fraction of `B(⁴He) = 28.295662 MeV`: it exceeds `35 %`\nof the total binding energy — three orders above the `~1 %` the N³LO four-nucleon\nforce is estimated to supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_target_exceeds_n3lo_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_target_exceeds_n3lo_bound","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L153-L159","doc":"**The GAP-9 magnitude claim, certified.** The corpus target `μ₄ = −4.591`\nin units of `B(D) = 2.224566 MeV` is `10.213 MeV`, which exceeds `34 ×` the\nN³LO four-nucleon estimate of `0.300 MeV`. Over `ℝ`, as a numeric statement must\nbe; this is a certification of the probe's arithmetic, not a structural theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.below_tjon_of_mu4_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.below_tjon_of_mu4_neg","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L140-L147","doc":"The converse direction, recorded so the equivalence is visible: a negative\nfour-body moment *is* the statement that `M(4)` undershoots the two-point\nprediction. Together with the previous lemma this makes \"below Tjon\" and\n\"`μ₄ < 0`\" the same fact, not two pieces of evidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_neg_of_below_tjon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_neg_of_below_tjon","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L131-L138","doc":"**Saturation alone forces `μ₄ < 0`.** If the four-body point falls below the\ntwo-point prediction — which is exactly what a saturating binding curve does —\nthen the four-body moment is negative. No four-body interaction appears anywhere\nin this derivation, so the *sign* of `μ₄` carries no four-body information. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.additive_higher_moments_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.additive_higher_moments_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L108-L123","doc":"**Exact pairwise additivity kills every higher moment.** If `M(A)` is `c`\ntimes the edge count `C(A,2)` at `A = 2,3,4`, then `μ₃ = μ₄ = 0`. Hence a\nnonzero high moment measures *non-additivity*, never by itself a `k`-body\nforce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_eq_zero_iff_tjon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.mu4_eq_zero_iff_tjon","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L98-L106","doc":"**The prediction is exact iff there is no four-body moment.** This is the\nformal content of \"no four-body parameter is required\": `M(4)` is determined by\n`M(2)` and `M(3)` precisely when `μ₄` vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.tjon_deviation_eq_mu4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.tjon_deviation_eq_mu4","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L91-L96","doc":"**The Tjon line in simplex form.** The deviation of `M(4)` from the two-point\nprediction is *exactly* `μ₄` — nothing else contributes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.tjonPredict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TjonSimplexForm.tjonPredict","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TjonSimplexForm.lean#L86-L89","doc":"The two-point (\"no four-body parameter\") prediction for `M(4)`, built from\n`M(2)` and `M(3)` alone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}